{
  "cost_convention": "The reduced search takes one prefix square root per negative target. Each classified coordinate requires a squared difference, a parity test, one floor division by the public factor floor, and one band endpoint comparison with a multiplication. An even difference additionally needs a trailing-zero count and a right shift. A passing odd part receives one gcd. The raw band method jumps intervals. Extra divisions used to compare removing only one factor of two or to identify example skips are recorded separately from the search. The hybrid uses one division to find the first continuous band per qualifying product. It counts each lane endpoint root and each comparison of two available stream heads. Once both lanes are continuous and their heads are adjacent, it tests consecutive unreduced differences. Its unused lookahead is generated before the first hit and incurs no gcd. For other targets it uses the per-coordinate classifier. Fermat counts tested midpoints, including the successful one.",
